{"agent_id":"pp3g-6l7c-examine-settle-task-working-issue-287-child-of-279","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:32:46.931798248Z","event":{"type":"IssueUpdated","uuid":"bdf95444-8d7f-4468-aaf7-e58a7e10f84b","description":"Re-validation trigger filed from #277 (C2-gap gap-closing execution), per G8 of the #277 plan.\n\nSCOPE: The C2-gap investigation conclusions (research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/c2-gap-investigation/report.md, #228) are valid for toolregistry 0.15.0 / mcp 2.0.0 ONLY. Option B (ToolRegistry client interception via MCPConnectionManager._call_persistent subclass) couples to a PRIVATE, version-bound internal (connection.py:97-111) with no compatibility guarantee, and the PoC duplicates its body (intercept_poc.py:86-103, incl. dropped logger.warning at connection.py:107).\n\nTRIGGER: any toolregistry or mcp (Python SDK) upgrade — patch, minor, or major — after which the following must be re-verified:\n1. connection.py:106 still catches bare Exception (no failure-class distinction added);\n2. _call_persistent still spans connection.py:97-111 with the same body — lock (101/108) + _ensure_connected (102) + try (103) + single call (105) + except Exception catch-all (106) + logger.warning telemetry (107) + _connect (109) + ONE immediate unconditional retry (111); NO backoff (verified 2026-08-08, #287: grep for sleep|backoff|delay|retry in connection.py matches only the line-107 telemetry string);\n3. register_from_mcp still hardcodes MCPConnectionManager at integration.py:323;\n4. mcp/client/session.py:1110 still raises the schema-validation RuntimeError verbatim;\n5. B2/B2b phase scripts still pass at 1 spawn/1 proxy/no reconnect with verbatim ErrorResult.\n\nARTIFACTS: research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/c2-gap-investigation/ (report.md §5.5, §8, §11; tests/phase_b2_poc.py, tests/phase_b2b_preabsorbed.py, tests/measure_poc_size.py; venv /tmp/toolregistry-venv). Re-validation runs: research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/c2-gap-investigation/logs/revalidation-2026-08-08/ (committed by #287).\n\nRATIONALE: private-internal coupling means the report reads as current while potentially being void after upgrade; this issue gives the re-run a durable trigger (hy3 S6/R7).\n\nAMENDED 2026-08-08 (#287): criterion 2 corrected to quote the actual _call_persistent body and explicitly state 'no backoff' (auditor #284 concern)."},"signed_by":"SHA256:JKpwJ49ThkNHZsB84ox9srVtgmUDJCX6b5dDT51Lyvs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgY9dNqYMbIY52mSbzOC6zVAFXiCUp2JLgbg0b66zhx34AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDo24PUlJ55HATcUNbV3jGHAMM97PT554kidr4m5oRAsQI/i2Q3s7wsQTVQ1rSM1OCJhHtu8Cy2dehfJO3knVAI="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-6l7c-examine-settle-task-working-issue-287-child-of-279","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:33:01.417782336Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"bdf95444-8d7f-4468-aaf7-e58a7e10f84b","comment_uuid":"2fdc9e89-a136-43e4-8073-5a3fd96821f6","author":"pp3g-6l7c-examine-settle-task-working-issue-287-child-of-279","content":"CORRECTED CRITERION 2 (settled by #287, 2026-08-08): the trigger's criterion-2 parenthetical was mis-specified — it named 'backoff' as part of the _call_persistent body; there is no backoff. The #279 description has been updated with this corrected text. Actual body, QUOTED from /tmp/toolregistry-venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/toolregistry/integrations/mcp/connection.py:97-111 (toolregistry 0.15.0 / mcp 2.0.0):\n\n  97: async def _call_persistent(\n  98:     self, name: str, arguments: dict[str, Any]\n  99: ) -> CallToolResult:\n 100:     \"\"\"Call tool using a persistent connection with auto-reconnect.\"\"\"\n 101:     async with self._lock:\n 102:         await self._ensure_connected()\n 103:     try:\n 104:         assert self._client is not None\n 105:         return await self._client.call_tool(name, arguments)\n 106:     except Exception:\n 107:         logger.warning(f\"MCP call to '{name}' failed, reconnecting and retrying\")\n 108:         async with self._lock:\n 109:             await self._connect()\n 110:         assert self._client is not None\n 111:         return await self._client.call_tool(name, arguments)\n\nBody elements (line-precise): lock at 101 and 108; _ensure_connected at 102; try at 103; assert at 104; first call_tool at 105; except Exception catch-all at 106; logger.warning telemetry at 107; _connect at 109; assert at 110; single retry call_tool at 111.\n\nNO BACKOFF — verified independently (grep for sleep|backoff|delay|retry|RETRY across connection.py returns exactly ONE match: the line-107 logger.warning telemetry string 'failed, reconnecting and retrying'). No time import, no sleep call, no exponential/linear delay, no retry counter. The retry is a single unconditional IMMEDIATE second call at line 111 with no delay.\n\nCorrected criterion 2 (as updated in the description): '_call_persistent still spans connection.py:97-111 with the same body — lock (101/108) + _ensure_connected (102) + try (103) + single call (105) + except Exception catch-all (106) + logger.warning telemetry (107) + _connect (109) + ONE immediate unconditional retry (111); NO backoff.'\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: verified against the CURRENT installed venv only (no cross-version differential — none exists at baseline). The interpreter-level assert at 104/110 is listed for completeness but was not exercised by the harness.","created_at":"2026-08-08T07:33:01.411262898Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:JKpwJ49ThkNHZsB84ox9srVtgmUDJCX6b5dDT51Lyvs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgY9dNqYMbIY52mSbzOC6zVAFXiCUp2JLgbg0b66zhx34AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAK8KdpKLqePnpXhsuDPa6erq1HvNNfSejBWJru/eNf6GtvXEyGpRe2Q7B68fj4fIkTWOT6DaP0l8cj8fGhrHwAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:JKpwJ49ThkNHZsB84ox9srVtgmUDJCX6b5dDT51Lyvs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgY9dNqYMbIY52mSbzOC6zVAFXiCUp2JLgbg0b66zhx34AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCqy7757BI5yAXxBZcqwpXKPIv6HXz5FufE1ESXtFoYPNp0j/n2KHDIh+avGqTN2eAx9nKGCW64Bc786ZVsWtQk="}
